what is devops
  devops is an integration b/w (software) development activity & IT operations. It has a set of practices,tools,and a culture that helps to deliver software faster,
  more reliably,and with better collaboration.
    
what is ci/cd
  ci stands for continuous integration,here the code is downloaded and build into an artifact by developers
  cd stands for continuous deployment/delivery after the code is build the artifact is deployed into qa server to undergo the process of testing by selenium testers and
  later it was deployed into the prod environment 
  this ci/cd is fully an automated proces  which reduces the errors ,improves consistency in delivery ,more reliable
    
difference b/w git & github

                     git                                                                    github

  it works on offline                                                    it works online
  it contains single meachine data                                       it contains different types of data from different sources/meachines
  used as a local repository                                             used as a remote repository
  cannot provide collaboration among teams                               provides collaboration among teams
  popularly used to connect to servers of ec2                            popularly used to project management,enhancing team collaboration,issue tracking
  git is a vcs,tracks & manages code                                     github is a cloud based platform that hosts git repositories
  commands git pull,git add,git commit                                   issues,actions,code review,collaborations

what is docker
    docker is a containerization tool that packages an app and its dependencies into containers, enabling consistent deployment across different environments
    docker is a platform used to develop,package,and run application in the form of containers

differ b/w docker & k8s
      
